id suspicion.\" [4069] \"The assumption of changing the numbers seems to jump too quickly,\" Nishikawa said. [4070] But Tomoe was not stumped, \"It's natural to arrange the meeting time at 7 o'clock. We parted ways with Sougen at around 6:30 on the Dragon Forest River. Although we don't know what he did afterward, if the meeting was really at 9 o'clock, there would be some issues, such as where Sougen was for the two and a half hours before that and what he did. If the actual meeting time was 7 o'clock, the problem would be solved.\" [4071] I pondered Fukumura's reasoning. Fei Island quickly concluded the following, \"So, it becomes 'the person who had no alibi at 7 o'clock and had an alibi at 9 o'clock is the killer,' right?\" [4072] \"Yes.\" [4073] Oyama interrupted Fukumura's enthusiastic explanation again. [4074] \"Brother, what's wrong with you?\" [4075] \"Hey! I still have some doubts to ponder.\" [4076] \"You're massaging, aren't you?\" [4077] \"Listen! There's evidence that the murderer put the note in the pocket of the person in question, right? Sorry, I may be too nitpicky, but the note could have been with the person all along. They might have met unexpectedly, so there was no need to give the written thing to the murderer, so the person in question just put the note in the pocket and carried it around!\" [4078] Tomei smiled slyly, as if there was something else to it, \"Evidence, well... there may not be physical evidence, but there is proof. Just now, I kept saying there was a leak and a leak, but it was actually about this. Hey, Inoue, where was the note found?\" [4079] \"From the pocket of the person in question.\" [4080] \"Which pocket?\" [4081] \"Jeans.\" [4082] \"Where on the jeans?\" [4083] \"The pocket on the butt.\" [4084] \"Right side or left side?\" [4085] \"This... the right side.\" [4086] Takano pointed at Yashiro, \"Isn't that strange? Yashiro's right shoulder hurts, so he probably can't even write well. You think, then, could he stuff something into the right buttocks pocket?\" [4087] \"Good job! I didn't notice that.\" [4088] \"It's not a matter of whether it can be done or not. It might be possible with some effort, but it shouldn't be necessary to endure the pain and intentionally put something in the buttocks pocket! The front pocket is empty and can be left there, or it can be put in a bag with a wallet.\" [4089] \"I see!\" Yashiro interjected. [4090] \"We overlooked this unnatural aspect. If we look at it from the perspective of observation and reasoning, we should have gone beyond the idea that Yashiro received the note from the culprit and brought it to the scene. Perhaps it was like that from the beginning! Even if Higuchi didn't prank and draw those things, we should have inferred that \"even if it's not written by anyone, it's definitely the culprit who left the note at the scene,\" but everyone missed this point.\" [4091] Wakatsuki-san took the stage! His statement can be seen as a sweeping away of the ugliness of the battle in the rain. Weeda seemed to agree with this. [4092] \"If everyone agrees with this, we will arrive at the conclusion that Yuri-sensei mentioned earlier, which is 'the person who has no alibi at 7 pm and has an alibi at 9 pm is the killer.'\" [4093] Oh no! The plane had just started a joyful flight, but the altitude began to decrease! Even if we all agree with Wakatsuki-san's reasoning, the conclusion that \"the person who has no alibi at 7 pm and has an alibi at 9 pm is the killer\" does not hold much meaning. There are many people in Sumisen village who fit this description. [4094] I tried to think about what I know. The first ones that fit are us three. Before Yuri-sensei came to invite us at 7:20 pm, we had no alibis; after that, we were with him at Fukuju. Although we know we are innocent, from the perspective of the police, we fit the description. This may harm us. Yuri-sensei's alibi is the same as ours, and Shirogane Jouji, the dreamy post office clerk, arrived at Fukuju before 9 pm and had no alibi before that. [4095] However, others are different. Baochuo Miyuki, Nakahara Kunio, and Nishii Akira have no alibis at 7 pm and 9 pm. But can people with weaker alibis be absolved of suspicion? I pondered. If the killer's actions were as Wakatsuki-san reasoned, it is also possible that an unexpected event occurred, causing the killer to miss the opportunity to make an alibi at 9 pm. Things are not as simple as Wakatsuki-san said. [4096] \"I think your idea is good, but this conclusion still does not seem to point to who the killer is!\" Miyuki's statement was very mild, giving Wang Yuezhou a pat on the back for his good performance. [4097] \"Although it's a pity, it seems to be the case.\" It seems that Wang Yuezhou also admitted it, \"However, I think the suspect range should be narrowed down.\" [4098] \"So, I and Wang Yuezhou and others are also in the range of suspicion.\" Yoshiro thought of this, \"And those who have no alibis at 7 o'clock and 9 o'clock, Mr. Nishii and Miss Bao, are outside the range. This is strange, isn't it? Er, I'm not trying to drag people who have been cleared of suspicion back into the circle of suspicion... but... it seems that being alone and having no half-baked alibis is still better!\" [4099] \"My head is spinning!\" Miyuki put her hand on her forehead as if to measure the temperature. [4100] 2\n[4101] \"It would be better to tell the police about the content of our conversation so far. I think Mr. Wangyue's pointing out that the note was put in the right back pocket by the one with a sore right shoulder has great value!\" [4102] After Yushi said this, Wangyue modestly said, \"The police will notice this point soon. They may not remember how sore the right shoulder of the one who put the note in the right back pocket was - it's hard to remember it all at once if you haven't seen it yourself.\" [4103] \"But, we've already discovered that point! I want to go all out to identify the real culprit!\