t's what I wanted to ask him. Hikari stayed in his hotel room from 4 pm until we went out together at 6 pm. He didn't go out to find anyone, and no one visited him. So, what I wanted to say was: \"Hikari couldn't have met the person he was talking to unexpectedly!\" [4122] What a waste of my trying to remember! I sighed, feeling something stuck in my chest. [4123] \"Wait...,\" I murmured softly so no one could hear. [4124] We all inadvertently overlooked an obvious thing. How did Hikari, who wrote the message to X, get it to X's hands? After writing the message, Hikari didn't meet anyone outside the hotel, did he? [4125] I couldn't hear any sound from anyone or anything. Because I finally felt that the truth was gradually approaching. [4126] 3\n[4127] How did Hikari manage to deliver the note to someone? I started with this question, asking everyone to think together. \"It's indeed strange. Why didn't we notice it before?\" Nishijima took up the question first. [4128] Indeed, why didn't we notice it before? [4129] \"Hikari wrote the message at four o'clock, and we left the hotel at six o'clock. During that time, Hikari didn't have any contact with anyone outside the hotel. What did he intend to do with the written note?\" [4130] In the end, it was Fujimori who gave the answer, \"Well, this... The message that says to meet at seven o'clock or nine o'clock would not have been written at four o'clock and still be in his hand by six o'clock. He could have just been daydreaming and the time for the appointment would have come.\" [4131]\"Yes, yes...!\" Right! [4132]\"This means that the secret meeting is not urgent. The meeting time is 7:00, and it may refer to the next day's 7:00!\" [4133]What? [4134]\"So, if the note is not given to the other person after 7:00 on the day it was written, the other person will misunderstand the date. That's why the note written at 4:00 is still in his hand by 6:00.\" [4135]No! Takano has completely lost track and didn't even notice the re