d his mind and discarded them, should be rare, right? Even if it's a love letter, you have to have some awareness when you seal it!\" [3615] \"Is that based on experience?\" [3616] \"Mind your own business! What do you think, Mr. Higashiyama?\" [3617] The teacher pondered, \"What does Miyuki think?\" [3618] \"Hmm, I understand what Tsukiyomi means.\" Miyuki's opinion seemed to give Tsukiyomi a boost, making him nod contentedly, but weaving a cold shower. [3619] \"I disagree! This is not a logical inference.\" [3620] \"I know. I'm still figuring it out.\" Tsukiyomi didn't back down. [3621] \"Figuring it out is fine. Do you want to hear my next inference?\" [3622] \"I have thought of... \" When he said this, Hoshino glanced at Noguchi for some reason. \"I just thought of a more natural hypothesis than 'discarding the letter you've written because you changed your mind.' That is... for Sagara, is it no longer necessary to deliver the letter he has written?\" [3623] \"So, he changed his mind and didn't want the letter?\" [3624] I can't see how this differs from my opinion. [3625] Hoshino smiled and shook his head. \"No, I'm not saying he doesn't want the letter. I'm saying that the act of sending the letter is no longer necessary.\" [3626] \"It's the same thing,\" said Ochiai. [3627] \"What are you talking about? You guy, you don't even know how to listen to someone's reasoning! When I say 'the necessity of sending the letter has disappeared,' I mean that the recipient unexpectedly appears in front of you. Understood?\" [3628] I suddenly understood, \"So, the recipient is Mr. Nishijima?\" [3629] I finally blocked Noguchi's serve and looked at Nishijima. He looked puzzled, as if he didn't understand why his name suddenly came up. It seems he still doesn't understand. [3630] \"Wait\u2026 Wait a minute! Yuki! This\u2026 What are you talking about?\" Ochiai seemed flustered, as if he had been left behind. [3631] Wakamatsu cleared his throat and began to explain to the other