ee a bleak future!\" Zhi Zi rubbed his neck and complained. [2345] 3\n[2346] \"Oh, right!\" [2347] A deep voice interrupted. Looking over, we saw Nao stroking his bald head, \"I have a question. Why did the killer have to kill Nogi? Shouldn't we examine the motive for the crime?\" [2348] He was right. It was a lapse of focus to forget about this. [2349] \"What do you think?\" Kikyo asked. [2350] Nao cleared his throat, \"Nogi was killed the day after he announced his engagement to his wife. Don't you find that timing significant?\" [2351] Because small rice mentioned the phrase \"engagement with his wife\" in a calm manner, it made Kikuko frown. \"Do you mean that Ono was killed because he was engaged to me?\" [2352] \"I think there is a connection,\" small rice continued fearlessly. \"After marrying his wife, Ono would have had the opportunity to reform Kumashimo village, in fact, he may have revealed his intentions in the conversation earlier. I noticed his intention to reform this place. I think he would have been kicked out of here after marrying his wife. Although I considered leaving before that situation occurred, someone probably had a different idea.\" [2353] \"What idea?\" [2354] \"Like the idea of 'not accepting being kicked out of here,' for someone who still wants to continue creating in Kumashimo village, Ono's existence was a big trouble.\" [2355] \"You mean... he killed him just because of that? Just for that reason?\" [2356]\"I think it's sufficient reason.\" [2357]\"But cutting off his ear after killing him, do you still think it's a sufficient reason?\" [2358]\"Isn't it quite reasonable in terms of timing?\" [2359]The chrysanthemum looked around at the people present, \"What do you think? What do the others think?\" [2360]If asked to explain the rationale, I would probably only be able to answer \"I don't know.\" For someone who has no experience in struggling with creation and has a home to go back to, there are some areas that are unimaginable. 