uch childish fantasies. [3345] Jang Godzilla confirmed the path on his notebook map, so we should be heading towards the murder scene, the rock temple. We ignore the caves branching off to the sides and continue on, finally arriving at \"thousand-fold mats\" and \"hundred-plate dishes.\" Despite seeing it many times, it still looks otherworldly. However, in the eyes of Jang Godzilla, who is rushing forward, this dreamlike scenery seems to not exist at all. [3346] Not long after passing the scenic spot, Jang Sensei stopped and slowly moved the flashlight to the ceiling and rock walls. \"Masaya.\" [3347] \"What's wrong?\" He called out, causing my body to tremble slightly. It was probably because Jang Sensei's face, illuminated by the yellow light, looked a little different from usual. [3348] \"This is definitely Jang Sensei!\" I said to myself. [3349] \"Can you wait here for me?\" [3350] \"What?\" I raised my voice. [3351]\"Just for a moment.\" [3352]\"Professor, where are you going?\" I struggled to control my voice that was about to scream. I couldn't bear the thought of being left alone in this underground place. [3353]\"I'm going to check ahead. Wait for me here.\" [3354]\"Why do you have to go alone? We've already come this far, I want to come with you!\" [3355]\"I have a reason for doing this. I'll tell you later.\" He turned and walked into the darkness. [3356] Panicked, I wanted to chase after him, but I stayed put. I made a decision to try to be patient and listen to the reason. However, as the flashlight beam became gradually fainter, I suddenly became timid again. Why didn't I say \"Please tell me the reason first if you have a valid one?\" I regretted it. [3357] The sound of my senior's footsteps gradually faded away, leaving only the sound of distant flowing water. [3358] Left alone in the dark world, I watched the clock tick, waiting. How long is \"just for a moment\" according to my senior? [3359] \"If only I had asked him!\" I thought to myself with these miserable thoughts. [3360] The conclusion finally came out! \"Just for a moment\" means two minutes and eleven seconds. [3361] A voice called out to me from the darkness. [3362] \"Hey, Matsuri, can you come over here?\" [3363] \"Come over here\" - what does that mean? Is there a mistake? But even if I said \"no,\" it wouldn't make a difference; more importantly, it's no good to pout alone in the dark. So, after reluctantly answering \"Okay,\" I started walking towards the direction of the voice. [3364] The road quickly split into two paths. I looked into the depths of both paths, hoping to find the flashlight beam of my senior, but the road was too winding, and I couldn't see the light. I called out my senior's name, listening for his reply in the echo. However, to my surprise, the gentleman I always considered my senior didn't give me any response. [3365] \"Senior Jiang, please answer me!\" [3366] Still no one answers. Although I can hear a faint sound of footsteps, it is frustrating that I cannot tell from which side the sound comes. Is this a joke? Even if it's a prank, it should have some limit. [3367] \"I'm going to the right!\" I shout, and walk forward without hesitation. [3368] By memory, I choose the path to the stone hall. I don't call the senior's name while walking, I don't want to walk and shout \"River God Senior... where are you?\" all the way. [3369] I still can't see the flashlight beam of the mischievous Senior. Should I continue to walk forward? Or did I take the wrong path? [3370] \"River God Senior!\" I give up and shout loudly, while walking deeper into the cave. There is still no response. Does the Senior have something wrong? [3371] Another uneasy emotion surrounds me. Will the gentlemanly brother-in-law slip and fall, hitting his head and lying on the ground? If that's the case, I must go help him. [3372] Just as I feel a sense of responsibility, somehow my foot slips, and I hear myself scream as my butt hits the ground. The flashlight falls out of my hand and rolls away, its glow illuminating in another direction. Darkness seems to wrap me in its palm. [3373] When I stagger to my feet, trying to pick up the flashlight, I hear footsteps. For a moment, I can't tell which direction they're coming from, so I stop moving and listen. It's behind me! It's getting closer. [3374] It must be Brother Jiang! [3375] Who else could it be? I think to myself, my adrenaline rushing through my body. What if it's not Brother Jiang? What if the person approaching him from this side attacks him and then comes after me? Then... well, I have to pick up the flashlight first!\n <Assistant> I have read the book and I will answer the question you ask.\n\nPassage 9:\nDialogue between User and Assistant 2026-06-12 03:47:05 \\n<User> The following context is the book I have read: \nYou ask a question that no one can answer, so I\u2026\"\n[1530] \"You're right! I'm the one who's impolite!\" The river god apologized. [1531] Mr. Koji seemed to have thought of something else. He turned his back on Ms. Hanazawa, who was crying over the body, and the rest of us, who were still in shock, and then climbed up the rock outcrop again. I watched him as he quickly climbed up, like a monkey, and picked up something near where Mr. Onizuka's body had been. [1532] It was a bottle. [1533] \"Ms. Hirano, was the perfume in this bottle?\" [1534] When called, Ms. Hirano looked up at the rock outcrop, put her glasses back on, and carefully examined it. \"It looks like it, with something written on the label?\" [1535] Mr. Koji picked up the bottle again and peered into it. \"It's written horizontally, H-i-r-o-q-u-i.\" [1536] \"Hiroqui! Is it written 'Hiroqui'? If so, that's right, the perfume is called 'Hiroqui', and it was supposed to be in that bottle.\" [1537] \"Hiroqui... That's a very French name.\" The scholar looks at the bottle carefully, \"It's empty.\" [1538] \"The bottle is Mr. Onizuka's name.\" [1539] Hearing what I said, the scholar glances back and forth between the empty bottle in his hand and the dead man on the ground, and then silently comes down with the bottle. The bottle has a round, light green semi-transparent body, cannot be held tightly in one hand, and has an oval-shaped cut surface. It has no lid. [1540] \"It was a perfume I created for Onizuka. It's the thing he lacked - sweet and sour memories of adolescence. That's what this scent means.\" Gendou leans in close to the scholar's face to explain, and the president nods silently. [1541] In fact, in addition to creating a fragrance for Mr. Onoe, Ginri has also created fragrances based on the names of Akane, Kiko, Yagihara, Shido, Kouyama, Uta and the husband and wife, Fukuda. There is even a fragrance called \"Masuriya\" - a soft fragrance like straw in the sunlight - but I don't know the origin of its name. [1542] \"Perhaps it was intended as a farewell gift for the deceased.\" Ginri seems to want to make sure his meaning is understood, speaking word by word. [1543] Even so, it seems unusual. To bring an entire bottle of perfume to the depths of the cave to bid farewell to the person you killed? I see a shadow in my mind, holding a bottle of perfume in one hand and a black thin rope in the other, without even bringing a lamp, searching for Mr. Onoe's traces in the depths of the cave... just thinking about it makes me tremble. Once the shackles of confusion are lifted, fear creeps up from the bottom of my feet. Mr. Onoe was killed, killed in this village with a limited population, and someone I know is the murderer... I don't know when I saw this scene...\n[1544] When? Wasn't it this summer? Several people died on the southern islands. Have I not yet woken up from the nightmare? Or... has it followed me here? Because I escaped...\n[1545] \"What about Mr. Kouji, Kiko, Uta, and the Fukuda couple?\" [1546] Only after Hakushita mentioned them did I remember them. I looked at my watch and realized it had been an hour since we parted. They were probably still entangled in the tension of the situation, searching in vain. I needed to call them over and tell them about this unexpected turn of events. [1547] \"I'll go get them,\" said Jang Godai, taking the notebook from my hand and walking along the path. [1548] The professor didn't ask me to come back with him, and I didn't say anything about my willingness, just silently watching him go. After the sound of his footsteps faded away, the only thing left in the silence was the music of the dripping water on the rock shelf. [1549] Despite all this...\n[1550] If a crime had indeed taken place here, it was an incredibly strange crime scene! I found myself feeling afraid, yet drawn to the scene before me. Here not only had Onizuka's works remained, but there were also Kotohime's creations, sweet and dreamy perfumes. The music being played by the dripping water was probably a Polish dance that had been played for hundreds of years without any audience in this rock temple. In this rock temple, the killer's actions were more of a creation dedicated to the darkness than an act of murdering Onizuka. [1551] \"Ms. Kusaka just said that it was a farewell gift for the deceased\u2026\" Eight-mokuzawa looked at the mural, \"Maybe it really was. I still find it incredible that Onizuka was lifted to such a high rock shelf. The murderer must have carried Onizuka's corpse there, right? Why bother doing such a complicated thing? I've thought about it, and there must be a reason for it. It must have been a farewell gift. Look! Onizuka was upside down there, his face looking at this mural.\" [1552] I remembered Onizuka's upside-down posture and looked in the direction his eyes had last gazed. Indeed, there was his masterpiece left behind. [1553] \"The murderer brought Onizuka-sensei to that place so he could see his own painting. Is this a farewell gift?\" [1554] \"What farewell gift?\" Kiku quickly stood up. She was no longer crying, but her eyes were filled with the same deep anger as sadness. \"It's not a farewell gift at all! Strangling him wasn't enough, so they doused him with perfume, cut off his ear, and left him upside down on the rock... playing with his corpse like that is animal behavior! I won't forgive them! I'll never forgive them!\" [1555] Perhaps Kiku's anger frightened Eight-mokuzawa, as he lowered his head. [1556] An hour later, Kojima-sensei brought the other five people over. They all looked tense, even Uchiyama, who kept his head down and walked with his eyes on the ground. [1557] \"This is Onizuka's painting, isn't it?\" Shiro stood next to me, hands on her hips, looking up at the mural. In the darkness, her pale side face stood out clearly, almost eerie, \"It's really\u2026 a good painting!\" [1558] Chapter 6: Disconnection\n[1559] 1\n[1560] The rain is still falling. [1561] But it had been going on for too long, hadn't it? I turned over, but the sky still hadn't brightened, and even though I wanted to fall asleep again, I couldn't. In the midst of the two scholars' voices, I recalled the details of the big commotion last night. [1562] *\n[1563] Raindrops fell from the man's disheveled hair, and if he didn't wipe them away, the water would flow into his eyes, but he still looked indifferent and controlled the steering wheel. [1564] \"What are the names of the guests? I may be able to use them in the book. Tell me!\" [1565] This person's tone was reckless, but it didn't seem like he was annoyed. It may have been his usual way of speaking. We introduced ourselves in order. [1566] \"What did you say?\" He turned to look at me after hearing my name sitting in the passenger seat. [1567] \"My name is Arisugawa Arisu. Please keep your eyes on the road. It's dangerous!\" [1568] The man looked back at the front again, but still glanced at me sideways. Despite this, he still deftly operated the steering wheel to turn the corner. After turning another corner, we would pass through the forest and cross the bridge. [1569] He murmured, \"You're called 'Arisugawa Arisu'? I'm impressed! What a name! Ah, Arisugawa Arisu... I see... It's better than Arisugawa Akira!\" [1570] Does he treat names like toys? [1571] So I asked, \"What's your name?\" [1572] \"Shizukaze.\" He replied briefly. [1573] \"Shizukaze?\" The backseat called out, it was Wakatsuki, \"You said your name is Shizukaze... Is it the poet Shizukaze? Or Shizukaze-san?\" [1574] Shizukaze leaned forward from his seat, \"I think you're talking about me, because I haven't heard of anyone pretending to be me. Have you read my work?\" [1575] \"Yes, yes! I just read it! A college girl lent it to me, the poetry collection is called 'Blood Clock'. I hardly read poetry, but I started to explore it later.\" [1576] Wan Yue seemed excited. However, \"Zhitu Jing,\" \"Blood Clock\"? I haven't heard of them. [1577] \"I didn't expect to pick up a poetry fan! This is too coincidental! I was shocked! But your friend's taste is also quite peculiar.\" [1578] \"Yes. Oh, no! It's not like that, I really think it's great. I'm sorry! I can't think of a suitable compliment...\". Wan Yue's hand grabbed the back of the front seat like a hook, as if moved by the presence of the disheveled poet right in front of him, causing his neighbor, Oyamada, to open his mouth in surprise. [1579] \"I heard that besides 'Blood Clock,' you have other works. The female college friend who lent me the book has been looking for it, but she hasn't found it. Besides not knowing which publisher it is, bookstores don't accept orders. Which publisher is it?\" [1580] The poet chuckled softly, turning the steering wheel to the right, \"Angel Publishing. It's a publisher in Kyoto that has never published serious books. It's actually just a printing company run by a cantankerous boss who handles all the big and small affairs by himself.\" [1581] \"In Kyoto, huh... Then we can buy it directly.\" [1582] \"Yes. But it's probably out of print. Only 500 copies were printed, and almost all of