ctures of the mansion from a distance and was kicked out by Hachisuka? But in reality, he was secretly taking pictures from the windows inside the mansion, which is quite unusual\u2026\"\n[1615] \"Hmm, your story is completely different from his\u2026\" That's all I replied, while the other two fell silent, probably thinking something was off. [1616] \"When you were questioned by Akagi, you said you were here to find a friend, but the photographer didn't mention it. He just yelled, 'Just took some pictures, give me my camera back!' - These are the things I heard from my companions, as I was hiding in the room at the time - That guy may have had a reason he couldn't tell you, so the one with the secret is actually the photographer. Maybe he has relatives in the village?\" [1617] \"No, we haven't heard of that\u2026 but we can't judge the situation now.\" [1618] \"Anyway, the culprit of the misunderstanding is that guy. He violated Akagi's taboo, causing obstacles to your meeting with Miyuki, and even considered you as accomplices. As a result, the villagers became enemies with you, and the person who answered the phone did not properly convey the message, leading to the commotion in the rain.\" [1619] \"I apologize for the inconvenience.\" - Takao sincerely apologized. [1620] \"No problem.\" - Shido unnaturally widened his eyes, \"There's nothing to apologize for. I haven't been this happy in a long time. Goodbye!\" [1621] The rearview mirror showed Yoshiro smiling. It seems we have reconciled with Yoshiro. [1622] \"Just rest well tonight. We'll start over tomorrow, and I'll pass on the message for you. I quite like you, although it doesn't happen often, it still happens occasionally.\"\n <Assistant> I have read the book and I will answer the question you ask.\n\nPassage 10:\nDialogue between User and Assistant 2026-06-12 03:47:05 \\n<User> The following context is the book I have read: \nThey want to know why I kept watch over the corpse all night.\" [3495] \"There's no place to go out at night around here, so it's unnatural to have an alibi!\" Miyuki said. [3496] It seems that Mei Mei also doesn't have an alibi. [3497] \"Did you stay at home after returning at 7 pm, Mei Mei?\" asked the hopeless. [3498] \"Yes. I prepared dinner when I got home and ate around 8 pm. After that, my parents watched TV, and I put aside the dishwashing work and read books and stared into space in my room. Even though my house is a small bungalow, my parents probably wouldn't notice if Romeo came to tempt me out.\" [3499] Compared to the first conversation with Mei Mei, she is much more open now, probably because it is easier to get along with peers of the same age. Almost no male peers of our age are seen in this village. [3500] \"You were alone in your room, so your alibi shouldn't stand. \"Hopeless said casually, \"Even if you propose that the three of us were together, the police won't believe your parents' testimony.\" [3501] The fragrance of Darjeeling tea, the pleasant sound of a spoon hitting a cup, and the relaxed conversation about the murder case. Although it was a long afternoon, the detectives must be out in the gloomy weather, trying to arrest the killer. [3502] \"Have you heard the news on the radio?\" [3503] Mei Mei mentioned the news that was broadcasted during our sleep. The news reported that \"Mr. Mori was possibly involved in a transaction and killed.\" [3504] Mr. Mori's attempt to get an exclusive interview with Ms. Senjyu was suppressed by the police. It's hard to imagine that the \"incident\" he got involved in has nothing to do with Mukumura village. [3505] \"The detectives are investigating everywhere in the village. This is the biggest commotion since the village was established, and even reporters have come to the village. Although they are asking around to find suspicious people, if there really is a suspicious person in the village, the news will spread quickly. It would be a good thing if someone could come forward as a witness,\" said Dr. Nakagawa. [3506] \"Did Mr. Sagihara and the villagers of Sumisen Village ever have a dispute?\" [3507] At my question, Doctor Nakazawa only replied with a \"hmm.\" The \"transaction\" Mr. Sagihara was involved in must surely be related to Mukumura Village. Although Mr. Sagihara had planned to write a letter to someone outside the village, no one entered the village from the outside. Moreover, Mr. Sagihara had not done anything to provoke the villagers. [3508] \"Have the police contacted anyone in Mukumura Village yet?\" Weichida asks Doctor Nakazawa and Miyuki. [3509] Doctor Nakazawa's face contorted, resembling a lion in a lion dance troupe. He suppressed a yawn and said, \"The police certainly want to make contact. Although the bridge is broken, the residents on the other side should not only be cleared of suspicion but may also provide important information. The problem is finding a way to make contact. If only the phone could ring! Moreover, it's said that the police have used a loudspeaker to call out several times on the riverbank, but they still haven't seen anyone from the other side. It's not impossible, considering that the large house is on the other side of the forest.\" [3510] However, before reaching the large house, there are several houses that seem to be inhabited, and the sound of the loudspeaker should be able to reach those houses. Could it be that Mukumura Village never responded to Sumisen Village's calls? [3511] I recalled the last phone call from Jouji-sensei. [3512] \"There's a problem\u2026\"\n[3513] What problem? Have they been unable to respond due to a troublesome problem? Gradually becoming uneasy, I heard Dr. Nakagawa's voice. [3514] \"Since there has been no response, the police will have to cross the river.\" [3515] \"Cross the river to the other side?\" I breathed a sigh of relief. \"Is that possible?\" [3516] \"It's not a steep valley, so it should be fine. Can't we ask the fire department for help? Throw a rope to the other side and then use something like a basket to cross the river. We'll have to cross to the other side to fix the phone too!\" [3517] \"Basket?\" [3518] It's like a ninja! I imagine Detective Fujisawa from Fujisawa City, muttering to himself and crossing the river valley with a basket made of rope. It's quite a comical scene. [3519] \"But even if we pull the rope, it should be difficult to cross if there's no one on the other side to respond. I wish they would appear on the other side\u2026\"\n[3520] \"Maybe they don't know the bridge is broken\u2026\" Miyuki said, leaning on her hand. [3521] That's hard to imagine. [3522] \u2014\u2014There's a problem\u2026\n[3523] The voice of Mr. Kawajiri rang out again. Damn it! What's the problem? Is someone injured or sick? But if that were the case, they would have called for help on the shore. What is it? Why are you not giving us more hints? I silently question Mr. Kawajiri, who is not present. [3524] \"Didn't Fei Island contact you?\" Mr. Nakahara asked. [3525] We three replied, \"No.\" [3526] \"He said he hoped you all would come over to play, meaning you and Mr. Nishimura.\" [3527] 3\n[3528] We didn't visit Fei Island's house because he came to the inn. [3529] That night, Fei Island, Mr. Nishimura, and Mei gathered in our room. It would have been too much to ask the innkeeper to send six dishes, so Mei and I prepared the snacks. [3530] \"I'm glad you suggested coming to the inn, it's been a big help. My house is always a mess, so it's better to talk here slowly. Anyway, let's raise a glass first!\" [3531] After opening the beer bottle, everyone poured a drink for the person next to them. Although we weren't very familiar with each other, in Mr. Nishijima's casual conversation, Mr. Westwell gradually opened up, and the atmosphere became lively. [3532] \"It must be hard being a novelist, even on vacation you have to work! How is that book going now\u2026\"\n[3533] \"I sent it out via express delivery today.\" 